Advantages of SRTF SchedulingMinimizes average waiting time by always selecting the process with the shortest remaining time.Short processes finish quickly, improving system responsiveness and throughput.Helps time-critical tasks get CPU attention earlier than longer jobs.Disadvantages of SRTF SchedulingLong processes may suffer starvation if short jobs keep arriving continuously.Accurate prediction of CPU burst time is difficult and often unreliable.Frequent context switching increases overhead and can reduce overall performance.
